    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** providing the clear anchor for the lineup; his 87.42 efficiency score is fueled by an elite xwOBA of 0.448 and a favorable matchup against Keider Montero. Joining him in the \"Elite\" tier is **Christian Yelich**, who benefits from an aggressive platoon advantage and the +10% order bonus from his leadoff spot, while **Junior Caminero** remains a must-start despite facing a formidable arm in Zac Gallen, as his dynamic platoon edge and order placement keep his value well into the high 70s. We are also leaning on **Colt Keith** as a high-floor play against Spencer Arrighetti, where a +16% boost from the pitcher's skill profile and strong platoon data elevate him to a 69.64 score, significantly outpacing his base projection.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Luke Raley**, who finished with a 45.39 score\u2014just shy of our active threshold. **Raley** was squeezed out primarily due to a negative platoon split against the southpaw Joey Cantillo and the optimizer\u2019s preference for the higher-upside profiles of **Kazuma Okamoto** and **Lars Nootbaar**. Meanwhile, we are closely monitoring the 35% rain risk surrounding **Caleb Durbin**; while his 55.95 score is solid, the atmospheric uncertainty makes him our most volatile asset today. We are also keeping a close eye on **Pete Crow-Armstrong**; despite a difficult matchup against Jacob Misiorowski (2.74 xERA), his elite speed profile and leadoff deployment secure him a spot in the outfield, as we prioritize stolen base potential above all else in our pursuit of category dominance.",
